 "notes": "95% C.L. combined upper limit on g_agamma from the five-dwarf MUSE analysis assuming the NFW profile (paper's reference scenario), taken from the blue 'This work' curve in the left panel of the summary figure (Fig. 5, summary_compare.pdf). Coupling convention matches the canonical one: L = -(1/4) g_agamma a F Ftilde, decay rate Gamma = g^2 m^3/(64 pi) (Sec. 3). Curve extracted from vector paths of the e-print PDF, calibrated with tick marks, and downsampled from ~2400 vertices to ~100 points by median binning in log g; the plotted limit is highly jagged (channel-to-channel noise), so the binned curve tracks the local level of the fluctuating bound. Channels near ~4.2 eV (masked sky-line region) have no constraint (curve off scale); those bins are omitted. Limit derived from DM decay in dwarf spheroidals (density from Jeans analysis), so no local DM density assumption and no rescaling applied.",
